WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:02.870
People think of
classical dancers

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:06.410
as like these perfect,
soft, fairy tale characters.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.810
And I've been asked
before, wouldn't you

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:11.180
want to be perfect?

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.550
Why would I keep doing this
if I were perfect at it?

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.690
It would be so boring.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.890
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.130
Having been a professional
for almost 20 years,

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:24.490
I want to bring
ballet to more people.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.130
Every human being
should experience dance

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.420
in some way at some point.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.980
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.290
In this MasterClass,
you will learn

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:35.840
a simple way of approaching
the ballet technique,

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.370
as well as all that it
takes to accept who you are

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.690
and embrace who you want to be.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:45.220
You're really in such
a vulnerable state

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.780
when you're with
someone on stage,

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.322
and you're experiencing
what you are.

00:00:48.322 --> 00:00:50.005
And then you also
have to be so free.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.980
The number one thing
is absolutely trust.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.860
Yay. It was good.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.680
[LAUGHS]

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.650
I didn't start ballet
until I was 13.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.100
I experienced a lot of
hardships from a young age.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.030
Speaking was terrifying.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:11.800
And so to find this language
through movement was like,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.500
oh, this has been the
missing link my whole 13

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.090
years of living.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.430
It wasn't until dance
came into my life

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.280
that it made me confident.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.010
Focus on your placement
principles as you move

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.732
to attitude on relevé.

00:01:25.732 --> 00:01:27.940
They will help keep you from
pitching your upper body

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:28.780
forward.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.356
[SIGHS] [LAUGHS]

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.800
 So I rotate in and,
then, there you go.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.620
When it comes to working
with a choreographer,

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:39.370
come in with the approach
of being a blank canvas.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.320
You're there to be molded.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.090
I went through a
really difficult time

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:46.930
where I started to believe
people's words that I

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.650
wasn't right.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:49.090
I wasn't good enough.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.460
It was a way of saying, you
don't have the right skin

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.960
color for dance.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.380
I could have walked away,
but I took it as fuel.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.120
Own your power and your voice.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.030
Do not let other people's
words define you.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:05.150
I'm Misty Copeland, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:08.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

